From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] FT: Preserve MTK driver station entries during reassociation

MTK AP SME creates a station entry when sending an FT authentication
response or installing a PTK for FT over DS. It stores the reassociation
request in that entry. Removing it before sending the response
deauthenticates the station and discards the saved request. A subsequent
station update does not recreate this state, so the driver cannot send
the response.

FT reassociation preserves the authenticated entry when MTK AP SME is in
use. Station parameters are updated through the existing set-station
operation.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -5159,6 +5159,7 @@ static int add_associated_sta(struct hos
 	const u8 *mld_link_addr = NULL;
 	bool mld_link_sta = false;
 	bool owe_assoc_req = false;
+	bool mtk_ft_reassoc = false;
 	u16 eml_cap = 0;
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
@@ -5218,7 +5219,20 @@ static int add_associated_sta(struct hos
 		wpa_auth_sta_key_mgmt(sta->wpa_sm) == WPA_KEY_MGMT_OWE;
 #endif /* CONFIG_OWE && CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MTK */
 
-	if (!owe_assoc_req && !mld_link_sta && !sta->added_unassoc &&
+#if defined(CONFIG_IEEE80211R_AP) && defined(CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MTK)
+	/*
+	 * MTK AP SME creates a STA entry during FT authentication or PTK
+	 * installation for FT over DS, then saves the reassociation request
+	 * in that entry. Removing it sends a deauth and discards the state
+	 * needed to transmit the reassociation response.
+	 */
+	mtk_ft_reassoc =
+		(hapd->iface->drv_flags2 & WPA_DRIVER_FLAGS2_MTK_AP_SME) &&
+		reassoc && sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_FT;
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211R_AP && CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211_MTK */
+
+	if (!owe_assoc_req && !mtk_ft_reassoc &&
+	    !mld_link_sta && !sta->added_unassoc &&
 	    (!(sta->flags & WLAN_STA_AUTHORIZED) ||
 	     (reassoc && sta->ft_over_ds && sta->auth_alg == WLAN_AUTH_FT) ||
 	     (!wpa_auth_sta_ft_tk_already_set(sta->wpa_sm) &&
